@startuml optimizer-lifecycle-state
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #607D8B
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}

title <b>Optimizer lifecycle and publication gate</b>\n<size:11><i>terminal outcomes cannot cross the publication boundary</i></size>

[*] --> Validated : validate typed signatures\nand rank-certified plan

state "Validated" as Validated #BBDEFB
state "Running" as Running #C8E6C9
state "Completed" as Completed #C8E6C9
state "Published" as Published #DCEDC8
state "Cancelled" as Cancelled #FFCDD2
state "BudgetExceeded" as BudgetExceeded #FFCDD2
state "Failed" as Failed #FFCDD2

Validated --> Running : start ready node
Running --> Running : start/finish workers\ncommit next canonical provenance
Running --> Completed : all nodes finished\nprovenance complete\nwitness present
Completed --> Completed : independent exact confirmation
Completed --> Published : witness present and\n(non-exact or exact-confirmed)

Validated --> Cancelled : cancellation
Running --> Cancelled : cancellation
Completed --> Cancelled : cancellation
Running --> BudgetExceeded : budget exhausted\nplan unfinished
Validated --> Failed : validation/runtime failure
Running --> Failed : validation/runtime failure
Completed --> Failed : validation/runtime failure

Published --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
BudgetExceeded --> [*]
Failed --> [*]

note right of Running #FFF59D
  Worker completion order may differ.
  Provenance commit order is canonical,
  so exact outputs are worker-count invariant.
end note

note bottom of Published #DCEDC8
  If precision is <b>Exact</b>, publication
  additionally requires an independent
  denotational confirmation.
end note
@enduml
